  "nl_text": "The rschema_0445 database is designed to manage personnel, units, and various records related to their activities. The database consists of 13 tables, each representing a distinct entity. The personnel table stores information about individuals, including their ID, name, type, contact phone, email, health status, entry permission, and the unit they belong to. The unit table contains details about the units, such as their ID, name, type, and the administrator in charge. The administrator table stores information about the administrators, including their ID, name, and management role. The health record entry table links personnel to their health records, while the access personnel table links personnel to access records. The access point entry table links access records to access control points. The appointment table stores information about scheduled appointments, including the ID, scheduled entry and exit times, status, visitor name, and the personnel being visited. The health record table stores health records for personnel, including the appointment ID, scheduled entry and exit times, status, and the personnel ID. The access record table stores access records for personnel, including the record ID, entry and exit times, personnel ID, and access control ID. The access control table stores information about access control points, including their ID, name, location, and status. The affiliation table links personnel to the units they belong to, while the management table links administrators to the units they manage. The visit appointment table links appointments to the personnel being visited. Each table has a primary key, and some tables have composite primary keys to ensure data integrity. Foreign keys are used to establish relationships between tables, with cascade delete and update rules applied to maintain consistency.",
  "gold_question": "The campus access control management system functions as follows. For personnel information management, the system maintains basic information for all personnel, with each person having a unique ID, name, personnel type (teacher, student, third-party personnel, visitor), contact phone number, email and other basic information. Each unit has a unique unit ID, unit name, unit type (secondary unit, third-party unit) and other information. Administrators in the system each have a unique administrator ID, name and management role. For health monitoring, the system records health information for each person, including temperature, symptoms, health code color and other data, while tracking personnel travel trajectory information. For visitor management, each visitor appointment record has a unique appointment ID and records visitor ID, visited personnel ID, scheduled entry time, scheduled exit time and appointment status (pending review, approved, rejected) and other information. Visitors initiate appointments by scanning WeChat QR codes, and visited personnel review and confirm through the WeChat platform. For access management, the system records all personnel access records, including access record ID, personnel ID, entry time, exit time and access control device ID information. Each access control device has a unique device ID, device name, device location and device status (normal, fault) information. The system uses dynamic QR codes and facial recognition technology for identity verification, and employs HTTPS encryption for secure data transmission.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0445.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0445\nCREATE TABLE `personnel` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_phone` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `health_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `entry_permission` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unit_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `personnel_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`unit_id`) REFERENCES `unit` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `unit` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `administrator_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `unit_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`administrator_id`) REFERENCES `administrator` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `administrator` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `management_role` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `health_record_entry` (\n  `personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `health_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`personnel_id`, `health_record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `health_record_entry_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`personnel_id`) REFERENCES `personnel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `health_record_entry_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`health_record_id`) REFERENCES `health_record` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `access_personnel` (\n  `personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `access_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`personnel_id`, `access_record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `access_personnel_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`personnel_id`) REFERENCES `personnel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `access_personnel_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`access_record_id`) REFERENCES `access_record` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `access_point_entry` (\n  `access_record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `access_control_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`access_record_id`, `access_control_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `access_point_entry_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`access_record_id`) REFERENCES `access_record` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `access_point_entry_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`access_control_id`) REFERENCES `access_control` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `appointment` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `scheduled_entry_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `scheduled_exit_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `visitor_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `appointment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`personnel_id`) REFERENCES `personnel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `health_record` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `appointment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `scheduled_entry_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `scheduled_exit_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `health_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`appointment_id`) REFERENCES `appointment` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `health_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`personnel_id`) REFERENCES `personnel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `access_record` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `entry_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `exit_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `access_control_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `access_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`personnel_id`) REFERENCES `personnel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `access_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`access_control_id`) REFERENCES `access_control` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `access_control` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `affiliation` (\n  `personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`personnel_id`, `unit_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `affiliation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`personnel_id`) REFERENCES `personnel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `affiliation_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`unit_id`) REFERENCES `unit` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `management` (\n  `administrator_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`administrator_id`, `unit_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `management_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`administrator_id`) REFERENCES `administrator` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `management_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`unit_id`) REFERENCES `unit` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `visit_appointment` (\n  `appointment_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `personnel_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`appointment_id`, `personnel_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `visit_appointment_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`appointment_id`) REFERENCES `appointment` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `visit_appointment_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`personnel_id`) REFERENCES `personnel` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
